**Approximate Pareto front** (non-dominated in modulus × pore fraction):
- High modulus / low pore fraction: ~936 bar / 0.27 (run1, single specimen, SD=0, unvalidated)
- High pore fraction / moderate modulus: ~421–468 bar / 0.40–0.44 (18-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s series)
- Balanced: ~658 bar / 0.31 (run6, clean), ~519 bar / 0.36 (17p5-19deg-90s-run3)

### Validation Status

**17p5-0add-18deg-75s-N2-1800s**: 6 runs total. Run1 (936 bar, PF=0.27, SD=0, single fit) is a large apparent gain but based on a single specimen with SD=0 — not reproducible. Run2 (675 bar, PF=0.30), Run6 (659 bar, PF=0.31) are more consistent. Runs 4 and 5 (Oct 30) failed to yield modulus/pore fraction. The reproducible mean across runs 2 and 6 is ~667 bar / 0.30–0.31 — this is a credible Pareto-front candidate at moderate pore fraction.

**18-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s**: Runs 1–5 show pore fraction 0.32–0.44, modulus 339–476 bar. This is the high-pore-fraction end of the Pareto front. Runs 3 and 5 show PF=0.44 and 0.40 respectively with modulus ~421–468 bar. Run 1 (original) had PF=0.39, modulus=477. This candidate has 5 independent runs — it is reproducibly high pore fraction but with variable modulus (CV often high, wrinkles common). The high-PF end is reasonably confirmed.

### Gap in the Pareto Front

The current Pareto front has:
- A high-modulus cluster (~650–940 bar) at PF ~0.27–0.31 (polymer_wt=17–17.5, bath_temp=18–19°C, N2, short wait)
- A high-PF cluster (~0.38–0.44) at lower modulus (~350–470 bar) (polymer_wt=17.5–18, bath_temp=15–17°C, no-N2, longer wait)

**The gap**: Is there a region with modulus ~500–600 bar AND pore fraction ~0.35–0.40 simultaneously? This would be a Pareto improvement over both clusters. Looking at the data:
- 17p5-17deg-NoN2-75s (run1): 487 bar / 0.33 — close but pore fraction modest
- 17p5-17deg-NoN2-75s (run2): 397 bar / 0.37 — lower modulus, higher PF
- 18-15deg-300s-NoN2-1800s: 488 bar / 0.35 — promising! Clean membrane, CV=0.02, good quality. Only 1 run.
- 17p5-15deg-200s-NoN2-1800s: 367 bar / 0.38 — lower modulus

**18-0add-15deg-300s-NoN2-1800s** (single run, Oct 31): Modulus=488 bar, PF=0.35, clean membrane, CV=0.02, good fit quality. This sits in the middle of the Pareto front gap and has not been independently reproduced. It is a strong validation candidate.

### Decision

The **18-0add-15deg-300s-NoN2-1800s** condition (polymer_wt=18, bath_temp=15, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=300, nitrogen=false, mixing_temp=65, pullcast_speed=10, nips_bath_wait_time=1800) produced a clean membrane with modulus=488 bar and pore fraction=0.35 in a single run. This is a Pareto-front candidate in the middle of the modulus–pore-fraction tradeoff space, with only one independent synthesis. Per the validation policy, this should be repeated before treating it as confirmed. The parameters are all within bounds and feasible.

